index 4479b53..c116e72 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,40 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Account settings and passkeys
+
+After password sign-in, readers are taken to `/devtools-times/account/settings`.
+The existing password service authenticates readers; passwords and service tokens
+are never stored locally. A server-side session lasts 24 hours and is rotated on
+sign-in. Account settings support passkey creation, nicknames, deletion, reader
+display names, and passkey sign-in. Removing the last key is allowed because
+password sign-in remains available.
+
+Use Node 22.13 or newer (Node 24 recommended). Accounts and verified public-key
+credentials are stored in SQLite at `.data/accounts.sqlite`; set `ACCOUNT_DB_PATH`
+to change the location. Keep this file **and Astro's session storage** on persistent
+storage. This storage configuration is for a single Node deployment; a service
+with multiple instances needs a shared account database and session driver.
+
+Set `WEBAUTHN_ORIGIN` to the public origin (for example, `https://example.com`)
+and `WEBAUTHN_RP_ID` to its hostname when deployed behind a proxy. Without these,
+the request origin and hostname are used. Production passkeys require HTTPS;
+localhost is supported for development. Credentials are scoped to their RP ID.
+
+The authenticated API at `api/account/passkeys` returns the complete credential
+list and public account details, never public keys or counters. PUT changes a key's
+nickname, DELETE removes an owned credential, and PATCH changes the reader's display
+name. All mutations check the request origin. WebAuthn challenges expire after five
+minutes and require user verification. Browser Signal APIs are feature-detected:
+the complete accepted list is sent after loading settings and after deletion;
+account display-name updates use `signalCurrentUserDetails`. Key nicknames are
+local labels. Unsupported or failed sync leaves server changes saved and explains
+how to update the password manager manually.
+
+Provider metadata in `src/lib/passkey-providers.json` is a small local subset of
+the [passkey AAGUID registry](https://github.com/passkeydeveloper/passkey-authenticator-aaguids).
+Unknown and zero AAGUIDs use a generic icon. This metadata is a display hint only.
+
+Run `pnpm test` for storage isolation, session protection, and browser sync tests;
+run `pnpm run build` for the production build.
